WEBVTT

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:16.576
Sorry.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:17.583
I didn't realize

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.346
that you'd been
assigned here today.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:20.648
I wasn't.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:22.314
This space was unoccupied,

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.118
so I came here to work.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:25.681
On what?

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.125
I'm reconfiguring
the power couplings

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.219
in this section.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.287
Why?

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:34.232
The Astrometrics Lab
requires additional energy.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.564
I see.

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:37.627
So you're rerouting power
from other locations

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.331
like... Engineering.

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:42.769
They are minor adjustments.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.834
Primary systems
will not be affected.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:46.140
Unless, of course,
someone is trying

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.908
to do a warp core diagnostic,

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.710
which my crew has been
trying to do all morning.

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:54.517
We have lost hours of work
because of this.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:56.784
There is no need for anger.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.950
I had no intention
of causing a problem.

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:02.325
What, "sorry" isn't
in the Borg vocabulary?

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.627
You need to check with me

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.599
before you touch
the power systems.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.295
Understood?

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:11.802
Understood.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:22.848
I am unaccustomed
to working in a hierarchy.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:23.974
In the collective,

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:26.281
there was no need
to ask permission.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.184
If you're going to be
a member of this crew,

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.313
get used to it.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:30.720
Procedures exist for a reason.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:31.985
We've got to work together.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.889
We follow
the same set of rules...

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.364
Lieutenant?

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:42.129
I was given that lecture once,

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:45.331
by Captain Janeway
when I first joined this crew.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.209
If I could adjust
to Starfleet life...

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:53.768
so can you.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.543
Of course.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.845
I am...

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.943
sorry for the inconvenience.

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:07.482
Doc, I've got to go
run a few errands.

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:08.494
I'll be back soon.

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:10.826
Not so fast, Mr. Paris.

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:11.956
Can't these errands wait

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.555
until the end
of your duty shift?

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.661
Uh... well, it's my conn report,
actually.

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:19.865
I just realized
I forgot to turn it in

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.874
and Chakotay gives me
a hard time when it's late.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:23.967
You've been here all afternoon.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.444
Didn't this occur to you before?

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:29.107
Well, we've been so... busy

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:31.913
that I guess it just
slipped my mind.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.985
I see.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:39.082
Well, since it's an emergency,
don't let me stand in your way.

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.558
Thanks.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:48.858
Sir.

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:10.053
Computer, lock on
to these coordinates.

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:12.182
I need
a site-to-site transport.

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:14.591
No, wait.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.959
Access the central
replicator files first.

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:21.431
Ah...

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.367
perfect.

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:40.743
Are those supposed to make up
for canceling on me last night?

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:43.187
I got stuck with an extra shift
on the Bridge.

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.588
What could I say...

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:47.184
"Sorry, Captain,
I've got a date with B'Elanna"?

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:49.889
And what about right now?

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:52.124
Aren't you supposed
to be working in Sick Bay?

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:54.895
I said I had to go
deliver a conn report.

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.424
Not bad.

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:58.835
But he'll be expecting you back.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.805
He can wait.

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:13.010
What is it?

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:17.522
I just had the feeling
that somebody was watching us.

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:19.718
I must be completely paranoid

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:23.490
about getting caught in
a compromising position.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.997
Kind of exciting, isn't it?

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:21.401
Your trapezius
is hard as a rock.

00:06:21.446 --> 00:06:22.470
You haven't been following

00:06:22.514 --> 00:06:24.277
the relaxation regimen
I prescribed for you.

00:06:24.316 --> 00:06:25.578
I've been too busy.

00:06:25.617 --> 00:06:26.948
The usual story.

00:06:27.018 --> 00:06:28.178
Have you been getting
enough sleep?

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:29.949
More or less.
Mostly less.

00:06:30.021 --> 00:06:32.683
Mm-hmm. And have your headaches
been getting any worse?

00:06:32.724 --> 00:06:35.659
No, but they're not getting
any better either.

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:38.720
They're like hot needles
driving into my skull.

00:06:38.763 --> 00:06:41.755
These symptoms are
hardly surprising, Captain.

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:43.427
You work absurdly long hours

00:06:43.468 --> 00:06:45.936
under constant stress,
eating on the run,

00:06:45.971 --> 00:06:48.405
without sufficient
exercise or rest.

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:51.705
Your body is crying
out for mercy.

00:06:51.743 --> 00:06:53.643
It certainly is right now.

00:06:53.678 --> 00:06:55.908
There must be some easier
way to do this, Doctor.

00:06:55.947 --> 00:06:57.608
A hypospray, maybe?

00:06:57.649 --> 00:06:58.980
Always looking
for the simple fix.

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:00.517
Sometimes there's
no substitute for

00:07:00.552 --> 00:07:03.419
intensive osteopathic
pressure therapy.

00:07:03.455 --> 00:07:05.423
You're fortunate
to have a masseur

00:07:05.457 --> 00:07:07.584
who can work all day
without tiring.

00:07:07.626 --> 00:07:09.218
Bridge to the Captain.

00:07:09.261 --> 00:07:11.491
Commander, unless
this is an emergency

00:07:11.529 --> 00:07:13.053
my patient is unavailable.

00:07:13.098 --> 00:07:15.293
I'm here, Chakotay.
What is it?

00:07:15.333 --> 00:07:17.563
We've reached the source
of those energy readings

00:07:17.602 --> 00:07:19.866
and I thought you'd like
to see what we've found.

00:07:19.905 --> 00:07:20.872
On my way.

00:07:20.906 --> 00:07:21.873
Captain...

00:07:21.907 --> 00:07:23.272
I know what you're
going to say, Doctor,

00:07:23.308 --> 00:07:24.673
but I can't neglect
my responsibilities.

00:07:24.709 --> 00:07:27.143
Actually, I was going to
suggest a change of outfit.

00:07:30.649 --> 00:07:32.583
Binary pulsars.

00:07:32.617 --> 00:07:34.778
The gravitational forces
between them are so intense

00:07:34.819 --> 00:07:36.684
that everything
within 50 million kilometers

00:07:36.721 --> 00:07:38.245
is getting pulled in.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:40.622
Don't worry.
We're well out of range.

00:07:40.659 --> 00:07:43.651
Gamma radiation levels are high,
but as long as we're careful

00:07:43.695 --> 00:07:45.993
I think we can collect
some invaluable data.

00:07:47.832 --> 00:07:49.800
Captain, am I boring you?

00:07:49.834 --> 00:07:51.597
I'm sorry.

00:07:51.636 --> 00:07:54.196
I guess I'm a little
too tired to concentrate

00:07:54.239 --> 00:07:55.968
on stellar phenomena
right now.

00:07:56.041 --> 00:07:59.533
I'll leave this project
in your capable hands, hmm?

00:08:08.954 --> 00:08:11.013
You wanted to see me,
Lieutenant?

00:08:11.056 --> 00:08:13.183
Yes. I'm trying to increase

00:08:13.224 --> 00:08:15.920
the efficiency
of the impulse drive,

00:08:16.027 --> 00:08:17.051
but I wanted to make sure

00:08:17.095 --> 00:08:18.426
that I wasn't compromising
helm control.

00:08:18.463 --> 00:08:19.930
Sensible precaution.

00:08:19.998 --> 00:08:21.124
I'd be glad to help.

00:08:21.166 --> 00:08:23.930
Good. All of the specs
are at my upper workstation.

00:08:27.572 --> 00:08:29.233
Then let's get started.

00:08:41.453 --> 00:08:43.284
Did you hear something?

00:08:43.321 --> 00:08:45.016
You always think
you hear something.

00:08:49.127 --> 00:08:50.685
Commander.

00:08:50.729 --> 00:08:52.196
Lieutenant.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:55.097
Here is the power usage data
you requested.

00:08:56.167 --> 00:08:57.259
Right. Of course.

00:08:57.302 --> 00:08:59.862
I didn't expect it
quite so... promptly.

00:08:59.904 --> 00:09:01.838
Which I guess I should
have, uh, coming from you.

00:09:01.873 --> 00:09:02.840
I mean, I'm grateful

00:09:02.874 --> 00:09:04.865
that you got the data
to me so quickly.

00:09:05.944 --> 00:09:06.933
Thanks.

00:09:19.557 --> 00:09:21.320
Tuvok.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:25.652
Tuvok, I guess that was
kind of embarrassing.

00:09:25.697 --> 00:09:27.426
I don't experience
embarrassment.

00:09:27.465 --> 00:09:29.023
Right.

00:09:29.067 --> 00:09:31.262
Well, then I guess
there's no harm done.

00:09:31.302 --> 00:09:32.360
It's not like there was

00:09:32.404 --> 00:09:33.928
a security violation
or anything.

00:09:34.005 --> 00:09:35.939
None that I am aware of.

00:09:35.974 --> 00:09:37.805
So, I guess there's nothing

00:09:37.842 --> 00:09:40.936
that would have to go
on any kind of report.

00:09:40.979 --> 00:09:43.174
You want me to conceal
what I've observed

00:09:43.214 --> 00:09:45.614
of your relationship
with Lieutenant Torres.

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:48.346
Well, I'd certainly
never ask you

00:09:48.386 --> 00:09:49.717
to be dishonest.

00:09:49.754 --> 00:09:51.881
Certainly not.

00:09:58.029 --> 00:09:59.963
Do you think he'll say
anything to the Captain?

00:10:00.031 --> 00:10:01.123
I don't know.

00:10:01.166 --> 00:10:02.929
Well, how did he sound?

00:10:02.967 --> 00:10:05.162
Annoyed? Amused?

00:10:05.203 --> 00:10:06.534
He sounded Vulcan.

00:10:06.571 --> 00:10:07.970
What more can I tell you?

00:10:08.039 --> 00:10:09.097
Deck 1.

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:12.303
We have got to be more
careful with appearances.

00:10:12.343 --> 00:10:14.573
We shouldn't go into the
briefing at the same time.

00:10:14.612 --> 00:10:15.704
Good idea.

00:10:15.747 --> 00:10:17.738
Okay, you go in first.
I'll come in a minute later.

00:10:17.782 --> 00:10:19.750
No. That'll look
even more suspicious.

00:10:19.784 --> 00:10:20.808
Listen to us.

00:10:20.852 --> 00:10:21.876
We're acting like criminals

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:23.387
when we haven't done
anything wrong.

00:10:23.421 --> 00:10:24.979
Well, I'm not saying
that we have.

00:10:25.056 --> 00:10:27.991
I just thought we wanted to keep
this relationship to ourselves.

00:10:28.026 --> 00:10:29.755
We do, right?

00:10:30.762 --> 00:10:31.956
Do you?

00:10:31.996 --> 00:10:33.190
If you do.

00:10:35.233 --> 00:10:37.463
Computer, halt turbolift.

00:10:37.502 --> 00:10:39.493
Let's figure out how we're
going to handle this.

00:10:39.537 --> 00:10:40.970
Well...

00:10:41.005 --> 00:10:42.996
I don't think that it's
anybody else's business

00:10:43.041 --> 00:10:44.633
how we feel about each other.

00:10:44.676 --> 00:10:46.007
Neither do I.

00:10:46.111 --> 00:10:48.136
Right, then we're agreed.

00:10:48.179 --> 00:10:50.443
We're just a little
more careful in public

00:10:50.482 --> 00:10:52.347
and we don't say
anything to anybody.

00:10:52.383 --> 00:10:53.782
At least for now.

00:10:53.818 --> 00:10:55.012
Now?

00:10:55.053 --> 00:10:57.453
Sounds like you see
a future in this.

00:10:58.756 --> 00:11:00.451
I would never be
so presumptuous.

00:11:00.492 --> 00:11:02.653
Smooth recovery, Lieutenant.

00:11:02.694 --> 00:11:03.683
I thought so.

00:11:03.728 --> 00:11:05.559
Computer, resume.

00:11:07.532 --> 00:11:09.500
So I'll go first,
and you follow.

00:11:09.534 --> 00:11:10.694
Right.

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:16.898
Here's the plan.

00:11:16.941 --> 00:11:18.203
We'll circle the two pulsars

00:11:18.243 --> 00:11:20.404
at a minimum distance
of 80 million kilometers.

00:11:20.445 --> 00:11:22.436
That might not be far enough.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:24.607
We've been detecting
some random proton bursts.

00:11:24.649 --> 00:11:26.139
A strong one could
knock out our shields.

00:11:26.184 --> 00:11:27.151
Tom, go to 90.

00:11:27.185 --> 00:11:28.846
Keep it a safe distance.

00:11:28.887 --> 00:11:29.979
Yes, sir.

00:11:30.054 --> 00:11:32.113
Tuvok, keep our shields
at maximum strength.

00:11:32.157 --> 00:11:34.785
Divert auxiliary power
if you need it.

00:11:34.826 --> 00:11:36.691
I want to take every precaution
on this survey.

00:11:36.728 --> 00:11:38.992
Report any problems immediately,
no matter how small.

00:11:39.063 --> 00:11:40.394
Dismissed.

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:43.662
Lieutenants Paris and Torres,

00:11:43.701 --> 00:11:45.726
I'd like to speak
with you for a moment.

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:47.465
Thanks.

00:11:53.011 --> 00:11:54.205
I don't usually pry

00:11:54.245 --> 00:11:56.805
into the personal lives
of my crew, but in this case,

00:11:56.848 --> 00:11:58.713
I have to question
your recent conduct.

00:11:58.750 --> 00:11:59.717
I guess Tuvok...

00:11:59.751 --> 00:12:00.718
Tuvok?

00:12:00.752 --> 00:12:02.219
I haven't heard a word
from Tuvok.

00:12:02.253 --> 00:12:05.154
But you two have been making
enough of a public display

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:07.124
that half the ship
is gossiping about it.

00:12:07.158 --> 00:12:08.785
Believe me, that wasn't
our intention...

00:12:08.826 --> 00:12:10.054
You are senior officers

00:12:10.094 --> 00:12:11.755
and I expect you
to maintain the standard

00:12:11.796 --> 00:12:12.854
for the rest of the crew.

00:12:12.897 --> 00:12:14.660
But this adolescent behavior

00:12:14.699 --> 00:12:17.167
makes me question my faith
in you both.

00:12:17.202 --> 00:12:20.399
If you choose
to pursue a relationship,

00:12:20.438 --> 00:12:21.962
that's your business.

00:12:22.006 --> 00:12:24.531
But you consider yourselves
under orders

00:12:24.576 --> 00:12:26.635
to use better judgment about it.

00:12:26.678 --> 00:12:27.906
Is that understood?

00:12:27.946 --> 00:12:30.073
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, Captain.

00:12:30.114 --> 00:12:32.048
Dismissed.

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:55.202
Computer, hot coffee... black.

00:13:35.413 --> 00:13:38.871
Commander Chakotay is suffering
bone decalcification,

00:13:38.916 --> 00:13:41.817
tissue necrosis,
decreased visual acuity...

00:13:41.853 --> 00:13:43.684
all classic signs of aging...

00:13:43.721 --> 00:13:44.983
but they've developed
within hours.

00:13:45.089 --> 00:13:46.579
Any theories?

00:13:46.624 --> 00:13:48.956
There's a rare genetic
disorder called progeria,

00:13:48.993 --> 00:13:51.359
which causes children
to age prematurely.

00:13:51.396 --> 00:13:52.988
But there's never
been an adult case

00:13:53.097 --> 00:13:56.498
and it was supposedly
eradicated two centuries ago.

00:13:56.534 --> 00:13:59.560
Even so, I took a close look
at your DNA.

00:13:59.604 --> 00:14:01.595
These segments regulate
your body's metabolism.

00:14:01.639 --> 00:14:02.936
My scans

00:14:03.007 --> 00:14:05.669
indicate that they've been
hyper-stimulated somehow.

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:06.938
What's the prognosis?

00:14:07.011 --> 00:14:09.775
I can't speculate on that
until I've identified the cause.

00:14:09.814 --> 00:14:11.543
There's no sign
of an infectious agent.

00:14:11.582 --> 00:14:13.948
We spent several hours
near a binary pulsar

00:14:14.052 --> 00:14:16.486
that was emitting
intense gamma radiation.

00:14:16.521 --> 00:14:17.510
Our shields were operating.

00:14:17.555 --> 00:14:19.284
I don't see how I could
have been exposed to it.

00:14:19.324 --> 00:14:21.292
At this point, we can't
rule out anything.

00:14:21.326 --> 00:14:23.624
I'm going to take a closer look
at the data we collected.

00:14:23.661 --> 00:14:25.822
We should also run
scans of my quarters,

00:14:25.863 --> 00:14:27.728
as well as my office
and the Bridge...

00:14:27.765 --> 00:14:28.789
everywhere I've been today.

00:14:28.833 --> 00:14:30.130
I'm not prepared

00:14:30.168 --> 00:14:31.863
to send you back
on duty yet, Commander.

00:14:31.903 --> 00:14:33.165
I may look pretty strange,

00:14:33.204 --> 00:14:34.728
but my mind is perfectly clear.

00:14:34.772 --> 00:14:36.797
I'd rather stay busy
than just sit here.

00:14:36.841 --> 00:14:38.934
I have no idea how your symptoms
will progress.

00:14:38.976 --> 00:14:40.967
You should remain
in Sick Bay for observation.

00:14:41.012 --> 00:14:42.604
He's right, Chakotay.

00:14:42.647 --> 00:14:43.739
I'll keep you informed.

00:14:43.781 --> 00:14:46.750
Whatever's affecting
the Commander's DNA

00:14:46.784 --> 00:14:48.979
is working
at a submolecular level.

00:14:49.087 --> 00:14:50.952
I'd like to set up
an electron resonance scanner

00:14:50.988 --> 00:14:52.580
in the Science Lab
to get a closer look.

00:14:52.623 --> 00:14:53.590
Use whatever you need.

00:14:53.624 --> 00:14:54.989
And ask B'Elanna
to give you a hand.

00:14:55.059 --> 00:14:56.185
Still having headaches, Captain?

00:14:56.227 --> 00:14:58.695
I don't need any more lectures
about working too hard, Doctor.

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:01.198
Chakotay's the one who needs
your attention right now.

00:15:01.232 --> 00:15:02.699
I'll get to work
on the scanner right away.

00:15:04.202 --> 00:15:06.033
"Under orders
to use better judgment"?

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:07.094
Well, that's pretty harsh.

00:15:07.138 --> 00:15:09.072
I hope I can manage it.

00:15:09.107 --> 00:15:11.098
Well, she does have a point.

00:15:11.142 --> 00:15:12.871
You could have been
more discreet.

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:14.343
Oh. I forgot I was talking

00:15:14.379 --> 00:15:16.370
to the most upstanding
Ensign in Starfleet.

00:15:16.414 --> 00:15:17.403
Good morning.

00:15:17.448 --> 00:15:18.415
Neelix.

00:15:18.449 --> 00:15:19.507
I was just about to whip up

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:20.812
a fresh batch
of scrambled eggs.

00:15:20.852 --> 00:15:21.819
Would you like some?

00:15:21.853 --> 00:15:24.287
Actually,
I was hoping you might have

00:15:24.322 --> 00:15:27.120
some leftover pleeka rind
casserole from last night.

00:15:27.158 --> 00:15:28.523
For breakfast?

00:15:28.559 --> 00:15:30.151
I like it.

00:15:30.194 --> 00:15:32.492
I'm sure I can
find some for you.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:36.967
So, I guess your relationship
isn't exactly a secret anymore.

00:15:37.034 --> 00:15:39.366
Do you think anybody on this
ship can keep a secret?

00:15:42.473 --> 00:15:43.997
Neelix!

00:15:46.344 --> 00:15:49.211
Aah... aah...
What's...

00:15:49.247 --> 00:15:50.214
what's happening?

00:15:50.248 --> 00:15:51.215
Paris to the Doctor.

00:15:51.249 --> 00:15:52.307
I'm bringing Neelix to Sick Bay.

00:15:52.350 --> 00:15:53.339
It's an emergency.

00:15:55.987 --> 00:15:58.649
Now pay attention, Mr. Paris.

00:15:58.689 --> 00:16:01.487
These scans should indicate
whether...

00:16:01.526 --> 00:16:02.720
Hmm.

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:03.920
What is it?

00:16:03.995 --> 00:16:05.929
It seems that your DNA
has been hyper-stimulated

00:16:05.997 --> 00:16:07.828
just like Commander Chakotay's.

00:16:07.865 --> 00:16:09.560
But Neelix doesn't
seem to be aging.

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:11.335
No. The effects
are quite different.

00:16:11.468 --> 00:16:14.801
If anything, I look...
like a Mylean.

00:16:14.838 --> 00:16:17.306
They occupy a region
of space near Talax.

00:16:17.341 --> 00:16:18.308
Interesting.

00:16:18.342 --> 00:16:21.937
Do Talaxians and Myleans
share a common ancestry?

00:16:21.978 --> 00:16:23.912
Not that I know of.

00:16:23.947 --> 00:16:25.380
Do the two races
ever intermarry?

00:16:25.415 --> 00:16:30.819
Yes. As a matter of fact,
my great-grandfather was Mylean.

00:16:30.854 --> 00:16:32.549
Then one-eighth
of your genetic material

00:16:32.589 --> 00:16:33.886
was inherited from him.

00:16:33.924 --> 00:16:36.051
Those must be the genes
which have become stimulated.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:39.956
Too bad my great-grandfather
wasn't a little better-looking.

00:16:39.996 --> 00:16:43.955
Hmm. As far as I can tell,
his condition seems stable.

00:16:44.034 --> 00:16:46.093
I'm going to leave you
in charge of Sick Bay

00:16:46.136 --> 00:16:47.797
so I can continue
the DNA analysis.

00:16:47.838 --> 00:16:50.102
If anyone else comes in,
I'll run a cellular scan.

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.835
Is there anything else I can do?

00:16:51.875 --> 00:16:53.399
Do your best
to keep them comfortable.

00:16:53.443 --> 00:16:54.501
Until we have more information,

00:16:54.544 --> 00:16:56.136
that's the best
either of us can do.

00:17:09.126 --> 00:17:10.650
Thought you might be thirsty.

00:17:10.694 --> 00:17:12.423
Thanks.

00:17:15.999 --> 00:17:18.126
Do you smell something strange?

00:17:19.903 --> 00:17:21.666
I... I'm...

00:17:21.705 --> 00:17:23.900
I'm afraid that's me.

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:26.272
I seem to be developing
Mylean sweat glands.

00:17:26.309 --> 00:17:27.401
Sorry.

00:17:27.444 --> 00:17:29.605
It's not so bad.

00:17:29.646 --> 00:17:33.673
Well, whatever happens,
I... I try to keep in mind

00:17:33.717 --> 00:17:34.877
that things could be worse.

00:17:36.787 --> 00:17:39.654
I still have my home
here on Voyager,

00:17:39.689 --> 00:17:40.951
my friends...

00:17:40.991 --> 00:17:42.458
Your hair.

00:17:42.492 --> 00:17:45.120
True, but I'd gladly lose it

00:17:45.162 --> 00:17:48.495
if I could have
my taste buds back.

00:17:48.532 --> 00:17:51.501
At least you're not
losing your eyesight.

00:17:51.535 --> 00:17:54.163
See that display over there?

00:17:54.204 --> 00:17:56.900
It's nothing but a blur.

00:17:56.940 --> 00:17:58.464
You think that's bad?

00:17:58.508 --> 00:18:02.000
The Doctor tells me my pupils
have dilated 60 percent.

00:18:02.045 --> 00:18:04.013
I can't even look at that
display, it's so bright.

00:18:04.047 --> 00:18:07.710
Yeah? Well, I've got
chronic arthritis in my fingers.

00:18:07.751 --> 00:18:09.742
I can barely
keep this glass steady.

00:18:09.786 --> 00:18:11.083
That's nothing.

00:18:11.121 --> 00:18:13.749
My spinal column
is fusing together.

00:18:13.790 --> 00:18:15.348
In a matter of days,
I won't be able to walk.

00:18:15.392 --> 00:18:16.620
Got you beat.

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:18.685
I can barely walk now.

00:18:20.063 --> 00:18:22.429
Lieutenant, can we help?

00:18:22.466 --> 00:18:23.490
I don't think so.

00:18:23.533 --> 00:18:25.091
I'm releasing you both
back to your quarters.

00:18:25.135 --> 00:18:28.798
I've just gotten reports
of more patients on the way.

00:18:28.839 --> 00:18:30.670
It's going
to get crowded in here.

00:18:30.807 --> 00:18:32.035
How's the scanner?

00:18:32.075 --> 00:18:33.337
Almost ready.

00:18:33.376 --> 00:18:35.901
Good. This disorder seems
to be spreading rapidly

00:18:35.946 --> 00:18:36.935
among the crew.

00:18:37.013 --> 00:18:38.605
Does that mean
we'll all be affected?

00:18:38.648 --> 00:18:39.876
Right now, it only means
that we need

00:18:39.916 --> 00:18:42.146
to find some answers
as quickly as possible.

00:18:42.185 --> 00:18:43.675
All right.
Give the scanner a try.

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:45.119
I'll start
with Commander Chakotay.

00:18:48.191 --> 00:18:49.783
How's the resolution?

00:18:49.826 --> 00:18:50.952
Very nice.

00:18:51.061 --> 00:18:53.461
Now, let's focus in
on the hyper-stimulated

00:18:53.497 --> 00:18:54.691
segments of his DNA.

00:18:54.731 --> 00:18:56.961
Can you give me
more magnification?

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:58.558
Coming up.

00:19:01.705 --> 00:19:03.195
That's odd.

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:04.298
What is?

00:19:04.341 --> 00:19:06.741
There seems to be
some kind of contaminant

00:19:06.776 --> 00:19:08.243
on the base pair sequence.

00:19:08.278 --> 00:19:10.644
It didn't show up
on the first scan.

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:12.910
I need a closer look.

00:19:12.949 --> 00:19:16.282
I'm going to maximum
magnification.

00:19:23.827 --> 00:19:25.089
What do you see?

00:19:25.128 --> 00:19:27.596
I'm not exactly sure.

00:19:27.631 --> 00:19:29.155
Well, what does it look like?

00:19:30.967 --> 00:19:32.628
See for yourself.

00:19:36.172 --> 00:19:38.800
I'm no microbiologist, but...

00:19:38.842 --> 00:19:40.776
that doesn't look
like it belongs there.

00:19:40.810 --> 00:19:42.368
Believe me, it doesn't.

00:19:42.412 --> 00:19:43.777
I've never seen
anything like it.

00:19:43.813 --> 00:19:45.508
This level
of submolecular technology

00:19:45.549 --> 00:19:47.813
is well beyond anything
Starfleet has developed.

00:19:47.851 --> 00:19:49.716
What are those markings?

00:19:49.753 --> 00:19:53.280
Some kind of alien writing?

00:19:53.323 --> 00:19:55.052
I wish I knew.

00:19:55.091 --> 00:19:57.491
They might help us
determine where it came from.

00:19:57.527 --> 00:19:59.461
But who could have put this
into Chakotay's cells

00:19:59.496 --> 00:20:00.485
without his knowledge?

00:20:03.867 --> 00:20:05.858
Let me try
a compositional analysis.

00:20:17.347 --> 00:20:19.941
It's in Mr. Neelix's DNA
as well.

00:20:19.983 --> 00:20:21.814
Is this what's causing
the mutations?

00:20:21.851 --> 00:20:25.082
A good scientist never jumps
to conclusions, Lieutenant,

00:20:25.121 --> 00:20:27.783
but I'd say
it's a distinct possibility.

00:20:28.992 --> 00:20:31.517
I'm having trouble getting a
clear reading from this sample.

00:20:31.561 --> 00:20:34.553
It looks almost like the, um...
whatever it is...

00:20:34.598 --> 00:20:36.793
could be slightly out of phase.

00:20:38.234 --> 00:20:40.498
That must be why my initial
scans didn't reveal it.

00:20:40.537 --> 00:20:43.700
I'm compensating
for the phase variance.

00:20:45.775 --> 00:20:47.367
You're not going
to believe this,

00:20:47.410 --> 00:20:49.401
but I'm picking up
an energy signature.

00:20:49.446 --> 00:20:52.381
This thing is transmitting
some kind of a signal.

00:20:52.415 --> 00:20:54.315
- To where?
- I don't know.

00:20:54.351 --> 00:20:56.114
It's too weak
to travel very far.

00:20:57.487 --> 00:20:59.512
Access the internal sensors

00:20:59.556 --> 00:21:02.218
and set them
to a phase variance of.15.

00:21:02.258 --> 00:21:03.316
Right.

00:21:06.496 --> 00:21:07.656
Lieutenant.

00:21:11.101 --> 00:21:12.568
Your program is being deleted.

00:21:12.602 --> 00:21:13.569
How?

00:21:13.603 --> 00:21:14.627
I don't know.

00:21:14.671 --> 00:21:16.298
I'm transferring you
back to Sick Bay.

00:21:21.344 --> 00:21:23.244
B'Elanna...

00:21:23.279 --> 00:21:24.303
Science Lab to the Bridge.

00:21:24.347 --> 00:21:25.336
This is the Doctor.

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:39.221
In the last hour,
three more patients have come in

00:21:39.262 --> 00:21:40.729
with genetic mutations.

00:21:40.764 --> 00:21:42.994
The effects are starting
to become life-threatening.

00:21:43.033 --> 00:21:44.227
What happened to B'Elanna?

00:21:44.267 --> 00:21:45.859
The alveoli in her lungs

00:21:45.902 --> 00:21:47.426
suddenly stopped
processing oxygen.

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:48.960
I've got her
on respiratory support.

00:21:49.005 --> 00:21:51.200
She almost died.

00:21:51.241 --> 00:21:53.334
What about the Doctor?

00:21:53.376 --> 00:21:55.003
The computer logs
in the Science Lab

00:21:55.045 --> 00:21:57.536
show that he was trying
to transfer himself to Sick Bay.

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:00.174
Something must have gone wrong
while he was in transit.

00:22:00.216 --> 00:22:01.444
Could the Doctor's program?

00:22:01.484 --> 00:22:03.475
Seven of Nine,
this is the Doctor.

00:22:03.520 --> 00:22:04.953
Can you hear me?

00:22:05.055 --> 00:22:06.886
It's me, the Doctor.

00:22:06.923 --> 00:22:09.050
I've tapped
into your audio implants

00:22:09.092 --> 00:22:11.185
so only you can hear me.

00:22:11.227 --> 00:22:13.354
It's imperative
that you tell no one.

00:22:13.396 --> 00:22:15.557
Make any excuse
to get out of there

00:22:15.598 --> 00:22:17.190
and report to Holodeck 2.

00:22:17.233 --> 00:22:19.394
I'm hiding
in the da Vinci simulation.

00:22:19.436 --> 00:22:21.233
I'll explain everything
when you get here.

00:22:21.271 --> 00:22:22.533
Seven was checking that.

00:22:22.572 --> 00:22:23.903
Seven?

00:22:24.908 --> 00:22:25.966
Seven?

00:22:27.911 --> 00:22:30.141
About the Doctor's research.

00:22:30.180 --> 00:22:33.946
Yes. I examined their work area.

00:22:33.983 --> 00:22:35.814
There was no record
of any findings.

00:22:35.852 --> 00:22:38.582
The electron resonance scanner
appeared to be malfunctioning.

00:22:38.621 --> 00:22:41.988
I... could return
to the Science Lab

00:22:42.025 --> 00:22:43.458
and attempt to repair it.

00:22:43.493 --> 00:22:45.484
Keep me informed.

00:22:49.032 --> 00:22:52.627
Hold your head this way,
Carlotta.

00:22:52.669 --> 00:22:55.399
I can only conclude
that someone has implanted

00:22:55.438 --> 00:22:57.872
these microscopic tags
in the DNA of the crew

00:22:57.907 --> 00:22:59.568
to cause genetic mutations.

00:22:59.609 --> 00:23:00.667
For what purpose?

00:23:00.710 --> 00:23:02.268
I don't know,
and I get the feeling

00:23:02.312 --> 00:23:03.745
they don't want us to find out.

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:05.475
Explain.

00:23:05.515 --> 00:23:07.483
When Lieutenant Torres
and I started making progress

00:23:07.517 --> 00:23:10.782
in our investigation,
we were both incapacitated.

00:23:10.820 --> 00:23:11.787
Call me paranoid,

00:23:11.821 --> 00:23:13.482
but I don't think
that is a coincidence.

00:23:13.523 --> 00:23:14.854
If you're correct,

00:23:14.891 --> 00:23:16.620
perhaps our actions
are being monitored.

00:23:16.659 --> 00:23:18.854
That's why I couldn't risk
contacting anyone

00:23:18.895 --> 00:23:19.919
over the com system.

00:23:19.963 --> 00:23:21.430
Our first course of action

00:23:21.464 --> 00:23:23.694
should be to collect
more information.

00:23:23.733 --> 00:23:25.758
My thinking exactly.

00:23:25.802 --> 00:23:29.966
B'Elanna wanted to adjust
the ship's internal sensors

00:23:30.039 --> 00:23:32.769
to a phase variance of.15.

00:23:32.809 --> 00:23:35.642
I'd like to do the same
to your Borg sensory nodes.

00:23:35.678 --> 00:23:37.339
Proceed.

00:23:37.380 --> 00:23:41.714
Computer, give me
a type-4 micro-inducer.

00:23:44.988 --> 00:23:46.319
Hmm.

00:23:51.161 --> 00:23:54.824
Now, take a look around,
and tell me what you see.

00:23:59.536 --> 00:24:01.800
Do you see anything...

00:24:01.838 --> 00:24:03.931
unusual?

00:24:03.973 --> 00:24:06.134
Energy signatures...

00:24:06.176 --> 00:24:10.738
or perhaps something that might
be transmitting a signal?

00:24:14.050 --> 00:24:15.347
No.

00:24:15.385 --> 00:24:16.477
That's one room down,

00:24:16.519 --> 00:24:18.419
256 to go.

00:24:18.454 --> 00:24:20.046
I suggest a deck-by-deck survey.

00:24:20.089 --> 00:24:22.922
If you need to contact me,
use com frequency Epsilon 2.

00:24:22.959 --> 00:24:24.756
I've isolated it
from the rest of the system.

00:24:24.794 --> 00:24:26.523
Understood.

00:24:27.831 --> 00:24:29.924
And be careful.

00:24:29.966 --> 00:24:32.161
Someone out there
could be watching.

00:25:16.980 --> 00:25:18.208
Deck 5.

00:26:13.501 --> 00:26:15.935
Computer, frequency Epsilon 2.

00:26:15.970 --> 00:26:18.803
Doctor, the aliens
are here on the ship.

00:26:18.839 --> 00:26:20.773
I can see them everywhere.

00:26:20.808 --> 00:26:22.503
This is worse than I imagined.

00:26:22.543 --> 00:26:24.306
You've got
to let the Captain know.

00:26:42.930 --> 00:26:44.693
Yes? Yes?!

00:26:46.567 --> 00:26:47.534
Good morning, Captain.

00:26:47.568 --> 00:26:48.967
That's a matter of opinion.

00:26:49.003 --> 00:26:49.970
What is it?

00:26:50.004 --> 00:26:51.938
Internal scans haven't revealed
anything

00:26:51.972 --> 00:26:53.371
about the genetic mutations.

00:26:53.407 --> 00:26:54.374
The Doctor?

00:26:54.408 --> 00:26:55.739
Still off-line.

00:26:55.776 --> 00:26:57.141
We are investigating
the possibility...

00:26:57.178 --> 00:26:58.975
Inform me of any progress.

00:26:59.046 --> 00:27:00.741
Understood.

00:27:00.781 --> 00:27:02.305
There's one more thing.

00:27:02.350 --> 00:27:04.284
The incident
with Tom and B'Elanna

00:27:04.318 --> 00:27:06.684
started me thinking
about ship's protocol

00:27:06.721 --> 00:27:08.814
or lack thereof.

00:27:08.856 --> 00:27:10.153
Captain?

00:27:10.191 --> 00:27:12.022
It seems to me that people
have been getting

00:27:12.059 --> 00:27:13.924
a little too comfortable
around here lately.

00:27:13.961 --> 00:27:15.656
They're late
for their duty shifts,

00:27:15.696 --> 00:27:18.927
taking Mess Hall privileges
during non-designated hours

00:27:18.966 --> 00:27:21.230
and a lot of people are spending
more time on the holodeck

00:27:21.268 --> 00:27:22.428
than they are at their posts.

00:27:22.470 --> 00:27:24.199
You are Security Chief.

00:27:24.238 --> 00:27:27.935
Don't 13 department heads
report to you every day?

00:27:28.008 --> 00:27:28.940
Yes.

00:27:29.009 --> 00:27:30.408
Well, straighten them out.

00:27:31.746 --> 00:27:34.112
Shall I flog them as well?

00:27:39.520 --> 00:27:41.579
Maybe the Doctor was right.

00:27:41.622 --> 00:27:43.419
I think I do need a vacation.

00:27:43.457 --> 00:27:45.391
You do seem unsettled.

00:27:45.426 --> 00:27:47.621
Crazed is more like it.

00:27:47.661 --> 00:27:50.630
I haven't felt this anxious
since my first day of command.

00:27:51.799 --> 00:27:53.630
Remind me to lower
the volume on that door.

00:27:53.667 --> 00:27:54.725
Come in.

00:27:56.003 --> 00:27:57.470
Captain, I wish to speak
with you...

00:28:00.908 --> 00:28:02.705
What's wrong?

00:28:04.779 --> 00:28:07.873
My attempts to repair the
resonance scanner have failed.

00:28:07.915 --> 00:28:09.314
I require assistance.

00:28:09.350 --> 00:28:12.581
Ask Ensign Kim
to lend you a hand.

00:28:14.088 --> 00:28:15.350
Yes, Captain.

00:28:16.357 --> 00:28:18.757
Is that all?

00:28:26.567 --> 00:28:28.125
When this mutation crisis

00:28:28.169 --> 00:28:30.364
is over, I think
I'll spend a few days

00:28:30.404 --> 00:28:32.634
in Renaissance Tuscany.

00:28:32.673 --> 00:28:35.369
There's a little inn
outside Sienna

00:28:35.409 --> 00:28:36.967
I've been wanting to try.

00:28:43.117 --> 00:28:46.484
I will join you
for a glass of wine.

00:29:03.103 --> 00:29:04.297
How many?

00:29:04.338 --> 00:29:06.203
I've observed 56 of the aliens.

00:29:06.240 --> 00:29:07.707
There could be more.

00:29:07.741 --> 00:29:10.232
Have you seen any pattern
to their behavior,

00:29:10.277 --> 00:29:12.905
any hint as to what they're
trying to accomplish?

00:29:12.980 --> 00:29:15.278
They seem to be conducting
experiments on the crew

00:29:15.316 --> 00:29:16.806
and monitoring the results.

00:29:19.453 --> 00:29:22.013
As if Voyager were
one big petri dish.

00:29:22.056 --> 00:29:23.455
I may be among them.

00:29:23.491 --> 00:29:25.925
In the turbolift, one of them

00:29:25.993 --> 00:29:28.518
probed me
with a medical instrument.

00:29:28.562 --> 00:29:30.723
We cannot allow them
to continue.

00:29:30.764 --> 00:29:34.200
I've been analyzing
their energy signatures.

00:29:34.235 --> 00:29:36.169
I believe there's a way

00:29:36.203 --> 00:29:37.727
to make them visible
to everyone.

00:29:37.771 --> 00:29:38.795
How?

00:29:38.839 --> 00:29:41.433
Using a precisely modulated
phaser beam.

00:29:41.475 --> 00:29:44.376
If we expose them, the crew
may be able to fight back.

00:29:44.411 --> 00:29:45.844
But what if the aliens
retaliate

00:29:45.880 --> 00:29:48.280
by inflicting lethal mutations
on everyone?

00:29:48.315 --> 00:29:49.304
It's too risky.

00:29:49.350 --> 00:29:51.318
What do you suggest?

00:29:53.787 --> 00:29:56.221
The key to the aliens' control
is the genetic tags.

00:29:56.257 --> 00:29:58.953
I believe a neuroleptic shock
would disable them.

00:29:59.059 --> 00:30:01.527
Unfortunately, it would be
rather... painful.

00:30:01.562 --> 00:30:03.359
Will the crew recover?

00:30:03.397 --> 00:30:05.524
Yes, they will.

00:30:05.566 --> 00:30:07.727
The hard part
will be administering the shock

00:30:07.768 --> 00:30:10.100
to everyone simultaneously.

00:30:10.137 --> 00:30:13.129
The power relays could be
reconfigured to do it.

00:30:13.173 --> 00:30:15.505
Good. I assume
you know how to do that?

00:30:15.543 --> 00:30:17.272
You assume correctly.

00:30:17.311 --> 00:30:19.973
But I will have to bypass
several safeguards.

00:30:20.014 --> 00:30:20.981
It will take time.

00:30:21.081 --> 00:30:22.810
Then you'd better get started.

00:30:57.985 --> 00:30:59.384
Tuvok to Seven of Nine.

00:30:59.420 --> 00:31:00.512
Yes?

00:31:00.554 --> 00:31:02.954
Why have you accessed
the EPS relay system?

00:31:03.057 --> 00:31:04.752
There is a malfunction.

00:31:04.792 --> 00:31:06.282
I'm attempting to repair it.

00:31:06.327 --> 00:31:08.625
Perhaps you should leave that
to the Engineering crew.

00:31:08.662 --> 00:31:09.924
Normally, I would.

00:31:09.964 --> 00:31:13.127
However, they are all occupied
with other tasks.

00:31:13.167 --> 00:31:15.635
You are compromising
the power safety protocols.

00:31:15.669 --> 00:31:17.296
Stop what you're doing at once.

00:31:17.338 --> 00:31:19.704
I assure you, there is
no cause for concern.

00:31:30.751 --> 00:31:32.878
Move away from the console.

00:31:37.458 --> 00:31:40.393
As I told you,
I am conducting repairs.

00:31:40.427 --> 00:31:42.952
You are attempting
to deceive me. Why?

00:31:48.769 --> 00:31:50.168
I can't explain what I'm doing,

00:31:50.204 --> 00:31:51.694
but you must allow me
to continue.

00:31:51.739 --> 00:31:54.264
Your actions could result
in an energy discharge,

00:31:54.308 --> 00:31:56.003
which would be
harmful to the crew.

00:31:56.043 --> 00:31:57.704
I realize that.

00:32:09.089 --> 00:32:10.078
Don't move.

00:32:11.392 --> 00:32:13.690
If your people attempt
to incapacitate me,

00:32:13.727 --> 00:32:15.160
I will kill you.

00:32:15.195 --> 00:32:16.992
I believe you.

00:32:19.133 --> 00:32:21.158
What do you intend to do now?

00:32:21.201 --> 00:32:23.863
You will come with me
to speak to the Captain.

00:32:23.904 --> 00:32:26.839
I am certain she will have
questions for you.

00:32:32.279 --> 00:32:34.679
Keep on trying
to disable the tags.

00:32:34.715 --> 00:32:35.807
Let me know when you're ready.

00:32:35.849 --> 00:32:36.816
Understood.

00:32:36.850 --> 00:32:38.818
I'll attempt to modify
the internal sensors

00:32:38.852 --> 00:32:40.217
to detect the aliens.

00:32:40.254 --> 00:32:41.243
Good.

00:32:41.288 --> 00:32:42.812
Keep me informed.

00:32:55.502 --> 00:32:57.493
Who are you?

00:32:57.538 --> 00:33:01.668
And what the hell
are you doing to my crew?

00:33:01.709 --> 00:33:04.872
My team has been observing you
and conducting tests.

00:33:04.912 --> 00:33:05.879
Tests?

00:33:05.913 --> 00:33:08.313
I'd call them mutilations.

00:33:08.348 --> 00:33:10.873
I can understand
why you're angry.

00:33:10.918 --> 00:33:12.852
I don't like causing
people to suffer,

00:33:12.886 --> 00:33:16.322
but sometimes it's
a necessary part of my work.

00:33:16.356 --> 00:33:17.914
What kind of work is that?

00:33:17.958 --> 00:33:19.425
Medical research.

00:33:19.460 --> 00:33:22.224
We're scientists, like you.

00:33:22.262 --> 00:33:26.221
From where I stand,
you're a hostile invasion force.

00:33:26.266 --> 00:33:28.461
I want to know
how long you've been here

00:33:28.502 --> 00:33:31.369
and exactly what
you've been doing to us.

00:33:31.405 --> 00:33:33.236
I can't answer those questions.

00:33:33.273 --> 00:33:34.968
It's a breach of protocol

00:33:35.075 --> 00:33:36.975
for me to be speaking
to you at all.

00:33:37.077 --> 00:33:39.170
Oh, how convenient.

00:33:41.081 --> 00:33:43.572
That way you never
have to face your victims.

00:33:43.617 --> 00:33:44.777
Captain, please.

00:33:44.818 --> 00:33:47.685
You're exaggerating
the situation.

00:33:47.721 --> 00:33:50.952
Our techniques are as benign
as we can make them.

00:33:50.991 --> 00:33:53.084
What I have been through
for the last few days

00:33:53.127 --> 00:33:55.254
certainly hasn't felt benign!

00:33:55.295 --> 00:33:58.662
Please understand that there's
a purpose to our actions.

00:33:58.699 --> 00:34:00.758
The data we gather from you

00:34:00.801 --> 00:34:03.793
may help us cure physical
and psychological disorders

00:34:03.837 --> 00:34:05.327
that afflict millions.

00:34:05.372 --> 00:34:08.398
Isn't that worth
some discomfort?

00:34:08.442 --> 00:34:10.307
I'm sure you'd see
things differently

00:34:10.344 --> 00:34:11.606
if your people were the ones

00:34:11.645 --> 00:34:14.113
being subjected
to these experiments.

00:34:14.148 --> 00:34:15.945
Just as your perspective
would change

00:34:15.983 --> 00:34:17.541
if your people were the ones

00:34:17.584 --> 00:34:20.212
to live longer
and healthier lives as a result.

00:34:20.254 --> 00:34:22.950
Don't forget, we've been
observing you, Captain.

00:34:23.023 --> 00:34:24.923
I know the most important
thing to you

00:34:24.958 --> 00:34:27.051
is the welfare of your crew.

00:34:27.094 --> 00:34:29.619
You'd even kill to protect them.

00:34:29.663 --> 00:34:31.631
If necessary.

00:34:31.665 --> 00:34:32.962
Of course you would.

00:34:33.033 --> 00:34:36.093
You take care of your own,
just as we do.

00:34:39.106 --> 00:34:41.973
We're really more similar
than you care to admit.

00:34:42.042 --> 00:34:43.703
That's where you're wrong.

00:34:48.715 --> 00:34:51.206
What you're doing
isn't self-defense.

00:34:51.251 --> 00:34:54.618
It's the exploitation
of another species

00:34:54.655 --> 00:34:56.179
for your own benefit.

00:34:56.223 --> 00:35:00.421
My people decided a long time
ago that that was unacceptable,

00:35:00.460 --> 00:35:03.657
even in the name
of scientific progress.

00:35:03.697 --> 00:35:07.155
You're a remarkably
strong-willed individual.

00:35:07.201 --> 00:35:10.136
I've been very impressed
by your self-control

00:35:10.170 --> 00:35:12.070
over the past several weeks.

00:35:12.105 --> 00:35:15.666
We've been increasing
your dopamine levels,

00:35:15.709 --> 00:35:17.836
stimulating various
aggressive impulses

00:35:17.878 --> 00:35:21.211
to test
your behavioral restraints.

00:35:22.482 --> 00:35:24.746
There's been a great
difference of opinion

00:35:24.785 --> 00:35:26.218
about how much more strain

00:35:26.253 --> 00:35:27.720
you can bear.

00:35:29.756 --> 00:35:31.121
Not much.

00:35:38.165 --> 00:35:39.792
I had hoped you might be
more cooperative

00:35:39.833 --> 00:35:41.960
once you realized
the importance of our work.

00:35:42.035 --> 00:35:42.967
Sorry.

00:35:43.036 --> 00:35:44.867
These lab rats
are fighting back.

00:35:44.905 --> 00:35:47.373
I'm afraid
that will be pointless.

00:35:47.407 --> 00:35:50.638
We're monitoring your attempts
to break our control over you.

00:35:50.677 --> 00:35:52.076
You won't succeed.

00:35:52.112 --> 00:35:54.478
Well, you may find that
you've underestimated us.

00:35:54.514 --> 00:35:57.142
Consider what's in the best
interests of your crew.

00:35:58.485 --> 00:36:00.919
We will be continuing
our research.

00:36:00.954 --> 00:36:03.223
If you make no further attempts
to interfere, I assure you

00:36:03.223 --> 00:36:05.623
If you make no further attempts
to interfere, I assure you

00:36:05.658 --> 00:36:08.354
that the fatality rate
will be minimal,

00:36:08.394 --> 00:36:11.192
though there may be
some deformities.

00:36:11.231 --> 00:36:15.167
And I would be willing to share
our final data with you.

00:36:15.201 --> 00:36:18.602
You can't possibly expect me
to accept that.

00:36:18.638 --> 00:36:20.697
If you don't,

00:36:20.740 --> 00:36:23.504
then the entire experiment,
and its subjects

00:36:23.543 --> 00:36:24.942
will be terminated.

00:36:32.218 --> 00:36:33.185
Are you telling me

00:36:33.219 --> 00:36:35.119
there is no way
to disable the tags?

00:36:35.154 --> 00:36:37.054
My attempts to use
the EPS relays

00:36:37.090 --> 00:36:39.183
to induce neuroleptic shock
have failed.

00:36:39.225 --> 00:36:41.125
The aliens may be responsible.

00:36:41.160 --> 00:36:42.889
I've encountered
similar difficulties

00:36:42.929 --> 00:36:45.090
in my efforts to modify
the internal sensors.

00:36:45.131 --> 00:36:48.362
They appear to have gained
access to our key systems.

00:36:48.401 --> 00:36:50.494
They can't be everywhere
all the time.

00:36:50.536 --> 00:36:52.800
We have got to find
an advantage.

00:36:52.839 --> 00:36:54.101
We'd better find one soon.

00:36:54.140 --> 00:36:55.869
Sick Bay is being filled
with new patients

00:36:55.908 --> 00:36:57.569
with increasingly
severe symptoms.

00:36:57.610 --> 00:36:59.976
We have the ability
to make them visible.

00:37:00.046 --> 00:37:02.412
If we could modify enough
sensors, we could resist them.

00:37:02.448 --> 00:37:05.178
They are still capable
of manipulating our DNA.

00:37:05.218 --> 00:37:07.311
A direct conflict
would be inadvisable.

00:37:07.353 --> 00:37:08.547
Bridge to Doctor.

00:37:08.588 --> 00:37:09.555
Medical emergency!

00:37:19.866 --> 00:37:21.356
She's in hypertensive shock.

00:37:21.401 --> 00:37:22.891
20 milligrams lectrazine.

00:37:22.935 --> 00:37:26.928
Her blood pressure is 360/125.

00:37:26.973 --> 00:37:28.736
How is that possible?

00:37:28.775 --> 00:37:30.208
Severe adrenal stress.

00:37:30.243 --> 00:37:32.507
No effect.

00:37:35.682 --> 00:37:37.809
Her arterial pathways
are rupturing.

00:37:37.850 --> 00:37:39.943
She's in cardiac arrest.
We're losing her.

00:37:43.156 --> 00:37:44.623
Captain, I'm afraid
that won't help.

00:37:44.657 --> 00:37:46.124
There's too much
internal bleeding.

00:37:46.159 --> 00:37:47.558
Then try something else.

00:37:47.593 --> 00:37:49.561
We'll transport her to Sick Bay.

00:37:49.595 --> 00:37:51.426
Her entire circulatory
system has collapsed.

00:37:51.464 --> 00:37:53.398
There's no way to repair
that kind of damage.

00:37:55.501 --> 00:37:57.332
Brain death has occurred.

00:37:57.370 --> 00:37:58.337
I'm sorry.

00:37:58.371 --> 00:37:59.929
There was nothing more
we could have done.

00:38:02.942 --> 00:38:06.070
This ends right now.

00:38:06.112 --> 00:38:07.909
You're relieved.

00:38:07.980 --> 00:38:10.847
Captain, what are you doing?

00:38:10.883 --> 00:38:13.374
I'm running a little
experiment of my own.

00:38:13.419 --> 00:38:14.750
Red Alert!

00:38:20.893 --> 00:38:23.555
Captain, one of the aliens
has just entered the Bridge.

00:38:23.596 --> 00:38:24.756
Understood.

00:38:24.797 --> 00:38:26.765
We're less than a million
kilometers from the pulsars.

00:38:26.799 --> 00:38:27.925
We must change course

00:38:27.967 --> 00:38:30.367
immediately to avoid being
caught in their gravity.

00:38:30.403 --> 00:38:31.870
No! Keep going.

00:38:31.904 --> 00:38:34.236
This is a far
more reckless course of action

00:38:34.273 --> 00:38:36.173
than I've come to expect
from you, Captain.

00:38:36.209 --> 00:38:37.676
It certainly is.

00:38:37.710 --> 00:38:40.508
Hull stress is at 30 teradynes
and rising.

00:38:40.546 --> 00:38:41.672
I'm transferring more power

00:38:41.714 --> 00:38:42.942
to the structural
integrity field,

00:38:43.015 --> 00:38:44.505
but I don't know
how long it can hold.

00:38:45.518 --> 00:38:47.645
What do you hope
to accomplish by this?

00:38:47.687 --> 00:38:49.814
Flying into a binary pulsar?

00:38:49.856 --> 00:38:51.790
It seems like I'm trying
to crush this ship

00:38:51.824 --> 00:38:53.257
like a tin can.

00:38:53.292 --> 00:38:54.259
It's more likely

00:38:54.293 --> 00:38:55.851
that you're trying
to intimidate us.

00:38:55.895 --> 00:38:58.227
You're welcome
to stick around and find out.

00:38:58.264 --> 00:39:00.323
Hull stress is at 45 teradynes.

00:39:03.403 --> 00:39:05.166
Our course is locked in.

00:39:05.204 --> 00:39:07.695
Only my authorization
can release it.

00:39:07.740 --> 00:39:10.106
You're not behaving
very rationally.

00:39:10.143 --> 00:39:13.772
That's what you were trying
to accomplish, wasn't it? Hmm?

00:39:13.813 --> 00:39:16.543
Pumping up my dopamine levels
to push me to the edge?

00:39:16.582 --> 00:39:18.311
Keeping me awake
for four days straight

00:39:18.351 --> 00:39:20.080
with the constant pain
of your devices

00:39:20.119 --> 00:39:21.552
drilling into my skull?

00:39:21.587 --> 00:39:23.885
Well, this is the culmination
of your work, and guess what?

00:39:23.923 --> 00:39:26.551
You're going to be right here
to collect the final data.

00:39:26.592 --> 00:39:28.651
Shields have failed.

00:39:28.694 --> 00:39:30.787
Structural integrity is down
to 20 percent.

00:39:30.830 --> 00:39:33.822
Enter the authorization code
and change course immediately!

00:39:33.866 --> 00:39:34.833
I don't think you realize

00:39:34.867 --> 00:39:38.132
that you are not
in control here anymore.

00:39:38.171 --> 00:39:41.140
I can kill you and your crew
in an instant.

00:39:41.174 --> 00:39:42.334
Go ahead.

00:39:42.375 --> 00:39:45.344
Without us, you won't be able
to prevent this ship

00:39:45.378 --> 00:39:47.039
from being torn apart
by the pulsars.

00:39:47.079 --> 00:39:48.842
And even with my crew
working together,

00:39:48.881 --> 00:39:50.746
I'd say the odds of us
getting through this

00:39:50.783 --> 00:39:52.444
are what? One in ten?

00:39:52.485 --> 00:39:54.544
One in 20, at best, Captain.

00:39:54.587 --> 00:39:56.817
I'm willing to take that chance.

00:39:56.856 --> 00:39:58.380
Are you?

00:39:59.559 --> 00:40:02.528
Outer hull temperature
has reached 9,000 degrees.

00:40:02.562 --> 00:40:04.029
The hull is beginning to buckle!

00:40:05.865 --> 00:40:09.062
Two alien vessels are attempting
to disengage from Voyager.

00:40:16.075 --> 00:40:18.976
I can't break us free
of the gravitational forces!

00:40:19.078 --> 00:40:21.876
Then let's divert all power
to the shields!

00:40:21.914 --> 00:40:24.075
No. If we go in,
we go in full throttle.

00:40:24.116 --> 00:40:25.276
Captain?

00:40:25.318 --> 00:40:26.342
Assuming we survive,

00:40:26.385 --> 00:40:27.977
we're going to need
all the momentum we can get

00:40:28.020 --> 00:40:30.113
to reach escape velocity
on the other side.

00:40:30.156 --> 00:40:32.249
Everyone, hang on.

00:40:33.659 --> 00:40:34.626
I hope you were

00:40:34.660 --> 00:40:36.753
exaggerating
about those odds, Tuvok.

00:40:36.796 --> 00:40:38.388
I was not.

00:40:43.135 --> 00:40:46.002
Hull stress has exceeded
maximum tolerance!

00:40:46.105 --> 00:40:49.472
There are breaches
on Decks 4, 7, 8 and 12.

00:40:49.509 --> 00:40:51.500
Emergency force fields
are holding.

00:40:51.544 --> 00:40:53.569
I've lost helm control!

00:40:53.613 --> 00:40:55.308
Main power is off-line!

00:40:55.348 --> 00:40:57.441
Well, let's hope
we've got enough speed.

00:41:09.662 --> 00:41:11.152
I don't believe it.

00:41:11.197 --> 00:41:12.960
We're alive.

00:41:13.065 --> 00:41:17.661
I never realized you thought
of me as "reckless," Tuvok.

00:41:17.703 --> 00:41:20.137
A poor choice of words.

00:41:20.172 --> 00:41:22.800
It was clearly
an understatement.

00:41:25.177 --> 00:41:29.136
Captain's Log, Stardate 51244.3.

00:41:29.181 --> 00:41:31.775
With the aliens gone,
the Doctor has been able

00:41:31.817 --> 00:41:33.842
to remove their devices
from the crew

00:41:33.886 --> 00:41:36.150
and neutralize the genetic tags.

00:41:38.357 --> 00:41:40.291
It was nice you could
get the night off.

00:41:40.326 --> 00:41:43.124
"Nice" had nothing
to do with it.

00:41:43.162 --> 00:41:45.323
I switched shifts
with Ensign Wildman,

00:41:45.364 --> 00:41:46.763
which means tomorrow

00:41:46.799 --> 00:41:49.597
I'll pull a double-duty
on the Bridge and with the Doc.

00:41:49.635 --> 00:41:52.433
Well, I appreciate
the sacrifice.

00:41:52.471 --> 00:41:55.304
Tell me about the wine.

00:41:55.341 --> 00:41:59.004
Ah, Ktarian merlot, 2282.

00:41:59.111 --> 00:42:01.636
You might want
to let it breathe first.

00:42:01.681 --> 00:42:03.876
We've got all night
to let it breathe.

00:42:03.916 --> 00:42:06.146
Engineering
to Lieutenant Torres.

00:42:06.852 --> 00:42:08.843
Torres here.

00:42:08.888 --> 00:42:11.083
We are having a problem
with the plasma manifold.

00:42:11.123 --> 00:42:12.818
I thought you'd want
to take a look.

00:42:12.858 --> 00:42:14.086
I don't.

00:42:14.126 --> 00:42:15.093
Lock it down for now.

00:42:15.127 --> 00:42:16.219
I'll deal with it
in the morning.

00:42:16.262 --> 00:42:17.524
Torres out.

00:42:17.563 --> 00:42:21.465
Sometimes it's nice to be
the Chief Engineer.

00:42:23.002 --> 00:42:24.697
Try the salad, Chief.

00:42:31.644 --> 00:42:32.668
Hmm.

00:42:37.083 --> 00:42:38.812
This is really delicious.

00:42:38.851 --> 00:42:39.943
Well, thanks.

00:42:39.986 --> 00:42:40.975
I replicated it myself.

00:42:41.053 --> 00:42:42.315
Mm, you're too good for me.

00:42:46.826 --> 00:42:48.088
Ignore it.

00:42:48.127 --> 00:42:49.594
Right.

00:42:53.199 --> 00:42:54.223
I'll get rid of them.

00:42:58.804 --> 00:43:01.102
Oh, hi.
Uh, sorry to interrupt.

00:43:01.140 --> 00:43:02.129
Hi, B'Elanna.

00:43:03.476 --> 00:43:04.875
Harry, I'm not home.

00:43:04.910 --> 00:43:06.070
I-I just wanted to return this.

00:43:06.112 --> 00:43:07.511
Thanks.

00:43:07.546 --> 00:43:09.514
Smells good.

00:43:11.117 --> 00:43:12.482
That's it.

00:43:12.518 --> 00:43:13.849
No more interruptions.

00:43:24.697 --> 00:43:28.895
You know, I've been thinking
about what the Captain said.

00:43:31.404 --> 00:43:34.134
Thinking maybe she was right?

00:43:35.241 --> 00:43:36.970
Me, too.

00:43:37.009 --> 00:43:38.874
We have been...

00:43:38.911 --> 00:43:40.640
a little out of control lately.

00:43:45.317 --> 00:43:47.080
Do you think we really were?

00:43:47.119 --> 00:43:48.143
What?

00:43:48.187 --> 00:43:50.087
Out of control?

00:43:50.122 --> 00:43:53.250
Those aliens could have
just been messing around

00:43:53.292 --> 00:43:55.487
with our hormones
just to see what would happen.

00:43:57.063 --> 00:43:59.224
You're right.
They could have.

00:43:59.265 --> 00:44:01.130
And we don't know how long
they were on board.

00:44:01.167 --> 00:44:03.260
They could have been
tampering with us for months.

00:44:03.302 --> 00:44:04.929
Well, when you think about it,

00:44:05.004 --> 00:44:07.302
you did have a pretty abrupt
change of heart

00:44:07.339 --> 00:44:08.533
a couple of weeks ago.

00:44:08.574 --> 00:44:12.601
What made you realize that
you loved me all of a sudden?

00:44:13.846 --> 00:44:15.711
Just a feeling.

00:44:20.086 --> 00:44:23.647
So, our whole relationship
might be based on some...

00:44:23.689 --> 00:44:25.623
alien experiment.

00:44:25.658 --> 00:44:28.491
You never know.

00:44:28.527 --> 00:44:30.654
Well, I think that explains it.

00:44:30.696 --> 00:44:34.860
I guess we should just...
call it off, then.

00:44:34.900 --> 00:44:37.198
I think so.

00:44:37.236 --> 00:44:39.568
Thank God we found out in time.

00:44:39.605 --> 00:44:40.970
Thank God.

